title: sony-s-dsp-python
message: >-
  If you use this work, or the states it was settled against, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Gustavo
    family-names: Franco
    alias: gufranco
repository-code: https://github.com/gufranco/sony-s-dsp-python
url: https://github.com/gufranco/sony-s-dsp-python
abstract: >-
  A model of the Sony S-DSP, the wavetable half of the SNES audio unit. Eight
  voices are pipelined across a thirty two clock schedule rather than run as a
  loop, which is what makes pitch modulation, key-on sampling, and the end-of-
  sample flag land where the hardware lands them. Settled against states taken
  from real music dumps with audio computed by a reference implementation, and
  nothing in it starts from a clean machine.
keywords:
  - emulation
  - super-nintendo
  - s-dsp
  - audio
  - adpcm
